Prism patch (2026-11-24): `hermes -z` (one-shot mode) honours agent.max_turns.

hermes_cli/oneshot.py builds its AIAgent without max_iterations, so AIAgent's default of 90 tool-calling
iterations applied in one-shot mode whatever config.yaml set under agent.max_turns (the interactive CLI and
gateway pass it through). The Prism demo / data-collection harness runs Hermes through `hermes -z`
(hermes_z.py), so the configured 120-call limit was silently 90.

Fix: oneshot reads agent.max_turns from the loaded config, falls back to the HERMES_MAX_ITERATIONS env var,
then to 90 (old behaviour), and passes it as AIAgent(max_iterations=...). Nothing else changes.
Base tree: hermes-agent c387be0 + hermes_prism_empty_recovery.patch + hermes_prism_browser_keepalive.patch.

--- a/hermes_cli/oneshot.py	2026-07-17 03:21:13.000000000 +0800
+++ b/hermes_cli/oneshot.py	2026-11-24 14:00:24.932616230 +0800
@@ -319,6 +319,14 @@
 
     cfg = load_config()
 
+    # Prism 2026-11-24: honour agent.max_turns. Stock oneshot built AIAgent without max_iterations, so
+    # AIAgent's default (90) applied whatever config.yaml said. Order: agent.max_turns, HERMES_MAX_ITERATIONS, 90.
+    _agent_cfg = cfg.get("agent") if isinstance(cfg.get("agent"), dict) else {}
+    try:
+        _max_iterations = max(1, int(_agent_cfg.get("max_turns") or os.getenv("HERMES_MAX_ITERATIONS") or 90))
+    except (TypeError, ValueError):
+        _max_iterations = 90
+
     # Resolve effective model: explicit arg → env var → config.
     model_cfg = cfg.get("model") or {}
     if isinstance(model_cfg, str):
@@ -396,6 +404,7 @@
         provider=runtime.get("provider"),
